  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "Our screen from database and reference searches captured 74 studies eligible for extraction, corresponding to 332 unique experiments investigating tumor volume response ( Figure 1 , Table 1 , Table 1—source data 1E ). Effect sizes (standardized mean difference [SMD] using Hedges' g) could not be computed for 174 experiments (52%) due to inadequate reporting (e.g., sample size not provided, effect size reported as a median, lack of error bars, Figure 1—figure supplement 1 ). Overall, 158 experiments, involving 2716 animals, were eligible for meta-analysis.",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study performs a meta-analysis of preclinical efficacy studies of sunitinib, involving a large number of experiments and animals. It quantifies effect sizes (SMD) and analyzes relationships between study design elements and these effect sizes, directly comparing animal model results. The study explicitly states 'in vivo animal studies testing the anti-cancer properties of sunitinib' and reports on 'experiments, involving 2716 animals'."
